  "query_preview": "(This evening through Thursday)...\nIssued at 153 PM EDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nSurface analysis this afternoon shows strong high pressure \nstretching from MN to IN, building SE. The upper flow was dominated \nby northwest flow aloft, stretching from the Pacific NW across the \nnorthern plains to the Ohio Valley. Water Vapor showed a stream of \nhigh moisture within this flow reaching Central Indiana. This was \nnot producing any precip within the region. Diurnal heating, mixing \nand ongoing subsidence has led to dew points to fall into the 40s.\n\nTonight and Friday...\n\nPleasant weather is expected tonight as the surface high pressure \npasses across Central Indiana before reaching the middle Atlantic \nStates on Friday. Forecast soundings tonight and Friday show a dry \ncolumn with unreachable convective temperatures. Thus expect \ncontinued mostly clear skies. Some high passing CI will be possible \nat times. Due to the low dew points, expect lows in the upper 40s \ntonight.\n\nSome warm air advection is noted on Friday as the surface high \ndrifts east and southerly flow develops within the lower levels. \nThis will lead to warmer highs in the lower 80s.\n\nSaturday...\n\nSome elements of the weather pattern will begin to change on \nSaturday. The NW flow aloft is expected to transition to ridging \nover the Mississippi and Ohio valleys. This will steer any upper \nlevel moisture north of Indiana. Overall a dry day is expected. \nHowever as the day progresses high clouds from hurricane remnants \nwill begin to arrive across Indiana from the south. This result will \nbe increasing cloudiness, especially notable in the afternoon and \nevening. Highs should once again reach the lower 80s with little \noverall change with the lower level airmass.\n\nForecast soundings on Saturday night begin to saturate toward 12Z \nSunday as cyclonic flow left from the hurricane arrives within the \nOhio Valley. Chances for showers late on Saturday night will need to \nbe included as forcing from this system arrives. Lows will only \nreach the upper 50s on Saturday night due to the arrival of a warmer \nand more humid air mass.\n\nSunday...\n\nHurricane remnants will be passing across Indiana on Sunday. Best \nmoisture and forcing looks to impact the southern and eastern halves \nof Indiana. This will lead to a rainy end to the weekend, especially \nduring the morning and early afternoon as the forcing dynamics pass. \nDry air and easterly progression of the system are suggested to \narrive by late Sunday afternoon and into Sunday night. This should \nbring an end to any rainfall.\n\nMonday...\n\nSome upper ridging and surface high pressure will bring quiet and \nwarm weather to the area on Monday. Highs will reach around 80 to \nthe lower 80s.\n\nTuesday onward...\n\nIt appears there will be enough influence from an upper trough \nmoving through southern Canada to push a cold front through the area \non Tuesday. Moisture looks to be limited so will only have some low \nPoPs. \n\nUncertainty remains on the details, but an upper trough across the \nwestern USA will create a surface low well northwest of central \nIndiana mid-week next week. An associated warm front will move into \nthe area and could bring some rain Wednesday and Thursday. With the \nuncertainty will keep PoPs low.\n\nHighs on Tuesday will reach around 80 before falling back into the \nlower and middle 70s Wednesday on the cool side of the front. Middle \nto upper 70s look likely on Thursday.",
